    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "People can now name patrons from their row, and each row shows its patrons and backing. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V22__person_patron.sql`, adds a `person_patron` table. The database itself rejects naming yourself or naming the same patron twice.\n- **Server:**\n  - A new endpoint, `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/people/{personId}/patrons`, takes `{patronId}`.\n  - It refuses yourself or a repeat with an error, and nothing is written when it refuses.\n  - When it succeeds it writes `PATRON_ADDED sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=<name> patron=<patron name>` to the audit file.\n  - The person list now includes each person's patrons, sorted by name. The new code is in `Patron.java`, `PatronRepository.java`, `PersonService.java` and `PersonController.java`.\n- **Front end (`people.ts`, `people.service.ts`):**\n  - Each row gets new fields: `person-patrons` (names joined by \", \") and `person-backing`.\n  - Each row also gets a `person-patron-select` dropdown and a `person-patron-add` button.\n  - A refused add shows `person-patron-error`. The error clears on the row's next action or when you change the dropdown.\n  - Backing is worked out on screen from the due-totals already shown. It adds up the patrons' due-totals, skips n/a, and shows 0.00 when there are no patrons. So it moves with holds, rate changes and date changes the same way due-totals do.\n\n**Choices I made where the request was open:**\n- The dropdown leaves out the person themselves, so you can't pick yourself on screen. Everyone else is offered, including people already named and retired people. Picking someone already named is refused by the server with the row error.\n- Patrons are sorted by plain character order, so upper and lower case sort separately.\n- Like hold, adding a patron doesn't check the user's role.",
